# Theme Blocks — Foundation Conventions

**Source of truth:** for current block syntax/APIs (`content_for`, `{% schema %}`,
static vs dynamic blocks, presets, targeting) query `shopify-dev-mcp`
(`learn_shopify_api` → `search_docs_chunks`). This file covers only
Foundation-specific conventions.

## Core Blocks

**Core Blocks** are atomic, pattern-library components prefixed `core-`
(`core-button.liquid`, `core-heading.liquid`, `core-text.liquid`, …). They are
the backbone of Domaine's storefront tooling.

- Core blocks may be edited directly when needed.
- When pulling updates from the foundation repo, manually sync changes to
  `blocks/core-*.liquid` — they are not auto-merged.

## CSS

- CSS exclusive to one block goes in that block's `{% stylesheet %}`, written in BEM.
- CSS reused elsewhere goes in `src/styles/_base.css` (shared `@layer base`/`components`), not the block.
- See [css-standards.mdc](css-standards.mdc).

